We're implementing GitHub issue #801 in the family-tree repo (React+TS frontend, FastAPI backend, but this issue is frontend-only).

## Issue #801
Title: "Documents tab: single click on a document should collapse/expand it"

Body:
In the member sheet's Documents section (`frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/MemberDocuments.tsx`), each document is rendered fully expanded — title, date, description, and the attached file list (`DocumentFileList`) are always visible. With several documents on a member, this section gets long and hard to scan.

Expected behavior: Clicking anywhere on a document's row (outside the edit/delete buttons) should toggle a collapsed/expanded state for that document — collapsed shows just the title (and maybe date), expanded shows the full description and file list, similar to how other collapsible sections in the app work (see `RecordSectionCard`, which `MemberDocuments` already renders inside, for the pattern to reuse).

Suggested approach:
- Add per-document collapsed state (e.g. a `Set<string>` of expanded document IDs, or default-collapsed vs default-expanded — worth confirming with design/UX) in `MemberDocuments.tsx`.
- Add an `onClick` on the row container that toggles the state, taking care not to trigger when the click originates from the Edit/Delete buttons (`e.stopPropagation()` on those buttons, as is likely already needed).
- Hide/show the description + `DocumentFileList` block based on the collapsed state.

Acceptance Criteria:
- [ ] Clicking a document row (not its buttons) toggles showing/hiding its description and file list
- [ ] Edit and delete buttons still work without triggering the collapse toggle
- [ ] Keyboard/a11y: row should be reachable and toggleable via keyboard too (e.g. `role="button"` + `tabIndex`/`onKeyDown`, or a dedicated disclosure control)
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` entry under `## [Unreleased]`

Relevant files: `frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/MemberDocuments.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/DocumentFiles.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/RecordSectionCard.tsx`

## What I already know (don't re-derive, just use it)

Current `MemberDocuments.tsx` (full contents, 142 lines):

```tsx
import { Member } from "@/types/member";
import { useDocumentStore } from "@/hooks/useDocumentStore";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { FileText, Plus, Pencil, Trash2 } from "lucide-react";
import { useState } from "react";
import { DocumentDialog } from "./DocumentDialog";
import { DocumentFileList } from "./DocumentFiles";
import { RECORD_SECTION_IDS, RecordSectionCard } from "./RecordSectionCard";
import { ConfirmDeleteDialog } from "@/components/shared/dialog/ConfirmDeleteDialog";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";
import { formatDate, sortByDateDesc } from "@/utils/dateUtils";
import { Document } from "@/types/document";

type Props = {
  member: Member;
};

export const MemberDocuments = ({ member }: Props) => {
  const { t } = useTranslation(undefined, {
    keyPrefix: "sheet.member-sheet.documents",
  });
  const { getDocumentsForMember, removeDocument } = useDocumentStore();
  const [isDialogOpen, setIsDialogOpen] = useState(false);
  const [editingDocument, setEditingDocument] = useState<Document | null>(null);
  const [documentToDelete, setDocumentToDelete] = useState<Document | null>(
    null,
  );

  const documents = sortByDateDesc(
    getDocumentsForMember(member.id),
    (doc) => doc.documentDate,
  );

  const handleAdd = () => {
    setEditingDocument(null);
    setIsDialogOpen(true);
  };

  const handleEdit = (doc: Document) => {
    setEditingDocument(doc);
    setIsDialogOpen(true);
  };

  const handleDeleteConfirm = async () => {
    if (documentToDelete) {
      await removeDocument(documentToDelete.id);
      setDocumentToDelete(null);
    }
  };

  return (
    <>
      <RecordSectionCard
        sectionId={RECORD_SECTION_IDS.documents}
        title={t("title")}
        headerActions={
          <Button size="sm" variant="ghost" type="button" onClick={handleAdd}>
            <Plus />
            {t("add")}
          </Button>
        }
      >
        {documents.length === 0 ? (
          <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground italic">
            {t("no-documents")}
          </p>
        ) : (
          <div className="space-y-2 mt-2">
            {documents.map((doc) => (
              <div
                key={doc.id}
                className="border rounded-lg p-3 hover:bg-accent/50 transition-colors"
              >
                <div className="flex items-start justify-between gap-2">
                  <div className="flex items-start gap-2 flex-1 min-w-0">
                    <FileText className="w-4 h-4 text-muted-foreground shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
                    <div className="flex-1 min-w-0">
                      <p
                        className="font-medium text-sm truncate"
                        title={doc.title}
                      >
                        {doc.title}
                      </p>
                      {doc.documentDate && (
                        <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                          {formatDate(doc.documentDate)}
                        </p>
                      )}
                      {doc.description && (
                        <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1 whitespace-pre-wrap">
                          {doc.description}
                        </p>
                      )}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div className="flex gap-1 shrink-0">
                    <Button
                      size="sm"
                      variant="ghost"
                      type="button"
                      onClick={() => handleEdit(doc)}
                    >
                      <Pencil />
                    </Button>
                    <Button
                      size="sm"
                      variant="ghost"
                      type="button"
                      onClick={() => setDocumentToDelete(doc)}
                    >
                      <Trash2 />
                    </Button>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div className="pl-6">
                  <DocumentFileList files={doc.files} />
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        )}
      </RecordSectionCard>

      <DocumentDialog
        open={isDialogOpen}
        onOpenChange={setIsDialogOpen}
        document={editingDocument}
        initialMemberIds={[member.id]}
      />

      <ConfirmDeleteDialog
        open={!!documentToDelete}
        onOpenChange={(open) => !open && setDocumentToDelete(null)}
        onConfirm={handleDeleteConfirm}
        title={t("delete-dialog.title")}
        description={t("delete-dialog.description")}
        cancelText={t("delete-dialog.cancel")}
        confirmText={t("delete-dialog.delete")}
      />
    </>
  );
};
```

There are TWO existing collapse patterns already in this same directory you should choose between (or blend):

1. `RecordSectionCard.tsx` — whole-section collapse, persisted in a Zustand store (`useMemberSheetSectionsStore`), keyed by a fixed `sectionId` string, uses `aria-expanded` on a `<button>` wrapping a `ChevronDown`/`ChevronRight` + title, toggles via `toggleSection(sectionId)`. This is for a small fixed set of section ids, not dynamic per-item ids, so probably NOT the direct model for per-document state (state doesn't need cross-render/component persistence here, just local `useState` should suffice) — but its visual/aria idiom (chevron rotates, `aria-expanded`) is worth matching for consistency.

2. `LinkedDocumentList.tsx` — per-list (not per-item, but structurally the closest existing "click to expand a details block" component in this exact domain) uses local `useState(false)` for `expanded`, a `<Button variant="ghost">` with `aria-expanded` and `aria-label` (translated show/hide), and a `ChevronDown`/`ChevronUp` icon that flips. This is single-item, not a per-row-in-a-list Set<string> pattern, but shows the idiomatic Button + chevron + aria-expanded/aria-label style this codebase uses for disclosure toggles.

Neither existing component demonstrates a `Set<string>` of expanded ids for a *list* of rows (which is what this issue needs, since there can be many documents, each independently toggleable). So the plan needs to design that state shape from scratch, following the visual idiom of the two components above.

Key project rules to respect (from AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md, already loaded into context — don't re-fetch):
- All user-facing text goes through i18next; new keys need entries in every locale file (there's an `npm run check-i18n` script that gates this in CI). Existing keys for this component live under `sheet.member-sheet.documents.*` (see `t()` calls above) — check `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/*.json` (or wherever the `documents` namespace file is) for the exact existing key file to extend, and enumerate ALL locale directories under `frontend/src/i18n/locales/` that need the new key(s) added.
- TypeScript strict, no `any`.
- Components only call Zustand store actions, never fetch directly — not relevant here since this is pure UI state, no new store needed most likely.
- CHANGELOG.md needs an entry under `## [Unreleased]` (create the heading if it doesn't exist — check current CHANGELOG.md head first).
- Don't over-abstract; this is a small, contained UI change.

## What to produce

A concrete, file-by-file implementation plan for a Sonnet engineer to execute directly (no ambiguity left to resolve at implement time). Specifically:

1. **State design decision**: What exact React state shape in `MemberDocuments.tsx` (e.g. `const [expandedIds, setExpandedIds] = useState<Set<string>>(...)`), and crucially: **default state** — should documents start expanded (matches current always-expanded behavior, least surprising) or collapsed (matches the issue's "scan a long list" motivation, and matches `LinkedDocumentList`'s default-collapsed precedent)? Make a call and justify it in 1-2 sentences; don't leave it open.
2. **Toggle handler design**: exact onClick placement, how to stop propagation from Edit/Delete buttons (inspect whether `stopPropagation` alone suffices given these are plain `<Button>` clicks, no nested forms).
3. **Accessibility**: exact markup for making the row keyboard-toggleable — decide between (a) making the whole row `role="button" tabIndex={0}` with `onKeyDown` for Enter/Space, or (b) adding a dedicated small disclosure chevron button (like `LinkedDocumentList`'s pattern) that's the actual interactive element, with the row's onClick as a secondary/redundant trigger. Pick one, justify briefly, and give exact JSX changes reflecting it — consider that nesting a `role=button` div containing real `<button>` elements (Edit/Delete) can be an a11y anti-pattern (nested interactive elements), so lean towards whichever avoids that if possible.
4. **Visual treatment of collapsed vs expanded**: what's hidden when collapsed (description + `DocumentFileList` per the issue; keep title + date visible), plus a chevron indicator so users can tell the state at a glance (reuse `ChevronDown`/`ChevronRight` from lucide-react, already imported pattern in `RecordSectionCard`).
5. **Exact diff-level description** of the new `MemberDocuments.tsx` — don't just describe it, write out the key changed JSX blocks so the implementer can transcribe them with minimal judgment calls.
6. **i18n**: exact new translation key(s) needed (if any — e.g. an aria-label for the toggle like "expand"/"collapse"), which JSON file(s) they go in, and instruction to add them to every locale directory under `frontend/src/i18n/locales/`. First inspect the actual locale directory structure and existing `documents` namespace keys before finalizing key names, so they match existing naming conventions (kebab vs camel, nesting depth).
7. **Test coverage**: is there an existing `MemberDocuments.test.tsx`? If so, note what test cases should be added/updated (row click toggles content, button clicks don't toggle, keyboard toggle). Locate the test file path.
8. **CHANGELOG.md entry**: exact line to add, matching the file's existing style (inspect the file's current `## [Unreleased]` section or most recent release section for tone/format).

Do the necessary file reads yourself (locale files, CHANGELOG.md, any existing test file) rather than asking me — I have NOT given you those contents. Output the plan as clear structured markdown, not code that will actually be applied (you are planning only, not implementing).

